A test application for user mode RDMA connection management.
The current code can only be used with IP addresses set to the RDMA NICS.
To run the code please follow the current steps:
1.  check that ib_ipoib module is installed:
	1.1 lsmod | grep ib
		and check if ib_ipoib is listed.  if not:
		1.1.1 modprobe ib_ipoib
			  and check that the module is listed
2. check that the NIC is shown
	2.1 ifconfig
		2.1.1 if the NIC is not shown call ibstat and check which port is ACTIVE
		2.1.2 port 1 is mapped to ib0 and port 2 is mapped to ib1
		2.1.2 ifconfig ib[0,1]
		2.1.2 ifconfig
			  and check that you can see the ib? in the list.  if there is no
			  address decide which address and call
			  example: ifconfig ib0 10.0.0.50/24
	2.2 call route and see that there is routing going through the RDMA NIC
	2.3 ping to the RDMA NIC address
3. on server side compile and run the app as follows:
	./cs
4. on client side compile and run the app as follows:
	./cs -s <server RDMA NIC IP>
5. see that the test completed
